            <ArticleTitle>Chest pain in pacemaker patients, the answer is not always antiplatelets and anticoagulants: a four-case series.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>347-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1742-6723.2010.01311.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chest pain in pacemaker patients can be difficult to evaluate due to alterations in QRS and ST segments on the surface ECG. A high prevalence of ischaemic heart disease in this population also serves to influence the differential diagnosis. We highlight four cases, all with simple yet informative imagery, in an attempt to alert clinicians of worrying signs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
